rde-fou RAM obligatoire). Utiliser avant un encodage, un remux, un réencodage, un batch d'images, ou dès qu'une tâche va faire tourner le CPU/GPU fort et longtemps. (file: r0/hardware-check/SKILL.md)\n- hatch-pet: Create, repair, validate, visually QA, and package Codex-compatible v2 animated pets from character art, generated images, company or prospect brand cues, or visual references. Use for any new Codex pet, custom mascot, non-pixel pet style, brand-inspired pet, existing-pet repair, or 8x11 spritesheet workflow requiring all 9 standard animation rows, 16 look directions, deterministic assembly, QA artifacts, and spriteVersionNumber 2 packaging. (file: r0/hatch-pet/SKILL.md)\n- interview-audio: Pipeline audio complet pour les musiques de fond et la voix d'une interview/vidéo. Télécharge une piste (yt-dlp, recherche ou URL) en WAV, applique fade in/out, et normalise — soit en normalisation CLASSIQUE (pic à un dBFS cible, ex -12), soit en LOUDNESS (loudnorm LUFS, ex -28 pour une BGM sous la voix, -16 pour la voix). Sait aussi extraire la piste audio d'un MP4 et lui appliquer une chaîne \"voix podcast\" (coupe-bas, chaleur grave, présence, compression douce, loudnorm -16). Utiliser dès que Matthieu veut préparer des musiques sous une interview, des SFX d'intro avec fades, normaliser des WAV à un niveau, ou traiter une voix en son podcast. (file: r0/interview-audio/SKILL.md)\n- kanji-stroke-order: Generate a textbook-style stroke-order diagram (SVG) for any Japanese character (kanji, hiragana, or katakana). Produces one panel per stroke showing completed strokes in black, the current stroke highlighted with a red number and directional arrow at its starting point, and remaining strokes ghosted in light gray. Use this skill whenever the user asks how to write a Japanese character, requests stroke order, asks \"in what order do I draw X\", wants to learn or memorize a kanji, asks to decompose a character into strokes, says \"show me the strokes for X\", mentions 書き順 / kakijun, or shows a stroke-order chart and asks for one for a different character. Trigger even when the user only provides a single charact (file: r0/kanji-stroke-order/SKILL.md)\n- kanji-stroke-order-html: Generate a complete standalone HTML study sheet for a Japanese kanji — stroke-order SVG inlined directly into the HTML body, plus a structured template with ON reading, KUN reading, stroke count, radical decomposition, mnemonic, 3-4 examples, and a sentence using the kanji. Produces a single self-contained .html file that opens correctly in any browser AND in Codex app's preview (no external file references). Use this skill whenever Matthieu learns a new kanji during his Japanese study sessions and needs the rich study sheet saved into Memory/Japanese/KanjiProgress/. For raw SVG without HTML wrapper, use the sibling skill `kanji-stroke-order-svg` instead. (file: r0/kanji-stroke-order-html/SKILL.md)\n- kanji-stroke-order-svg: Generate a standalone textbook-style stroke-order SVG for any Japanese character (kanji, hiragana, or katakana). Produces one panel per stroke — completed strokes in black, current stroke highlighted with red number and directional arrow, remaining strokes ghosted in light gray. Use this skill when the user wants ONLY the stroke-order diagram as a raw SVG (no HTML wrapper, no metadata). For the full HTML kanji study sheet with ON/KUN/mnemonic/examples bundled in, use the sibling skill `kanji-stroke-order-html` instead. (file: r0/kanji-stroke-order-svg/SKILL.md)\n- masterclass-builder: Use this skill to design rigorous, deep masterclasses and multi-module curricula (roughly 90 minutes per module, extensible to 15-20h) that build durable understanding and autonomous capability, not passive \"AI slop.\" Trigger this whenever the user wants to create a masterclass, a course, a deep curriculum, a structured learning program, progressive exercises on a topic, a study plan, or wants to genuinely LEARN a domain (not just get a one-shot answer), even if they do not use the word \"course.\" Covers learner profiling, 80/20 syllabus design, mechanism-level explanation (why before how), scaffolded progressive exercises, active recall, decision-forcing outputs, multi-agent adversarially verified research, (file: r0/masterclass-builder/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-knowledge-capture: Capture conversations and decisions into structured Notion pages; use when turning chats/notes into wiki entries, how-tos, decisions, or FAQs with proper linking. (file: r7/notion-knowledge-capture/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-meeting-intelligence: Prepare meeting materials with Notion context and supplemental research; use when gathering context, drafting agendas/pre-reads, and tailoring materials to attendees. (file: r7/notion-meeting-intelligence/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-research-documentation: Research across Notion and synthesize into structured documentation; use when gathering info from multiple Notion sources to produce briefs, comparisons, or reports with citations. (file: r7/notion-research-documentation/SKILL.md)\n- notion:notion-spec-to-implementation: Turn Notion specs into implementation plans, tasks, and progress tracking; use when implementing PRDs/feature specs and creating Notion plans + tasks from them. (file: r7/notion-spec-to-implementation/SKILL.md)\n- pdf:pdf: Read, create, inspect, render, and verify PDF files where visual layout matters. Use Poppler rendering plus Python tools such as reportlab, pdfplumber, and pypdf for generation and extraction. (file: r8/pdf/26.709.11516/skills/pdf/SKILL.md)\n- presentations:Presentations: Create or edit PowerPoint or Google Slides decks (file: r8/presentations/26.709.11516/skills/presentations/SKILL.md)\n- reduce-echo: Répare un enregistrement audio/vidéo (appel, interview, visio) qui souffre d'écho ou de réverbération causés par une double capture audio — typiquement un micro qui recapte le son sorti des enceintes, ou deux chemins audio mixés dans la même piste avec un délai